<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Auto clock-out - Timecard Portal</title>
    <%- headTags %>
</head>
<body>
    <%- include('partials/nav') %>
    <h1>Auto clock-out</h1>
    <p class="sub">If someone forgets to clock out, the portal closes the shift for them. It is checked every few minutes.</p>
    <% if (flash) { %><div class="msg <%= flash.bad ? 'bad' : 'ok' %>" role="status"><%= flash.msg %></div><% } %>

    <form class="panel" action="/admin/autoclock" method="POST">
        <h3>Settings</h3>
        <label style="display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center"><input type="checkbox" name="enabled" value="1" <%= cfg.enabled ? 'checked' : '' %> style="width:auto;margin:0"> Close forgotten shifts automatically</label>
        <label for="mh">Default shift limit (hours)</label>
        <input type="number" id="mh" name="max_hours" min="1" max="16" step="0.25" value="<%= cfg.maxHours %>" required>
        <p class="hint">The most hours credited for one shift. You can give a person their own limit on their Edit account page. A longer shift is allowed, but only the limit shows on the timecard until a supervisor approves the extra time (up to 5 minutes over is counted automatically).</p>
        <label for="wh">Extra time before a forgotten shift is closed (hours)</label>
        <input type="number" id="wh" name="window_hours" min="0" max="12" step="0.25" value="<%= cfg.windowHours %>">
        <p class="hint">People can keep working past their limit for this long. A shift still open after the limit plus this time is treated as forgotten and closed at the limit. Set 0 to close right at the limit.</p>
        <label for="co">Daily cutoff time (optional)</label>
        <input type="time" id="co" name="cutoff" value="<%= cfg.cutoff %>">
        <p class="hint">For example 15:30 if the school day ends then. A shift is closed at the cutoff or the longest-shift limit, whichever comes first. Leave blank to use only the longest shift.</p>
        <button type="submit">Save</button>
    </form>

    <div class="panel">
        <h3>Recently closed automatically</h3>
        <% if (!recent.length) { %><p class="hint">Nothing yet.</p><% } else { %>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table>
            <thead><tr><th>When</th><th>Person</th><th>What happened</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody><% recent.forEach(r => { %><tr><td><%= r.at %></td><td><%= r.target_name %></td><td><%= r.details %></td></tr><% }) %></tbody>
        </table></div>
        <% } %>
        <p class="hint">Managers can fix a time on Edit timecards. Each automatic clock-out is also in the Audit log.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
